# LOAD-BEARING — do NOT delete or disable. The wildcard address=/_dns-sd._udp/
# in local.conf does NOT cover these: dnsmasq routes by longest-suffix match, so
# names like db._dns-sd._udp.sub1.corp.internal match server=/sub1.corp.internal/
# (corpvpn-corporate.conf) and get forwarded to CorpVPN over TCP — a ~4700 qps
# storm that exhausts the 20 TCP-child limit and EPIPEs the CorpVPN DNS socket.
# Each entry below is a FULL suffix (address=/<sub>._dns-sd._udp.<domain>/) that
# out-specifies the forwarder and sinks the query locally to 0.0.0.0.
#
# Block mDNSResponder DNS-SD discovery storms for all CorpVPN-injected search domains.
# Regenerate when the search-domain list changes:
#   scutil --dns | grep SupplementalMatchDomains   (source of the <domain> list)
# Subtypes blocked per domain: lb/b/db/r/dr._dns-sd._udp
